Review written to `docs/reviews/physics-constants/phys-const-12-watts-per-ton-refrigeration.md`.

**Summary**: 1 low-severity finding — the `W_PER_TON` constant literal `3_516.852_842_066_667` compiles to an f64 1 ULP above the true nearest value. The ASHRAE derivation (12,000 BTU_IT/h) yields 3516.852842066666…, whose nearest f64 is `0x40ab79b4a7b721f9`. The recommended fix is changing the literal to `3_516.852_842_066_666_7`. OCHRE (via Pint) computes this correctly; EnergyPlus has no authoritative constant.
